BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:129925083@www.shadysideacademy.org
DTSTAMP:20261118T195632Z
DTSTART:20261030T193000
DTEND:20261030T220000
SUMMARY:Senior School Fall Play: CLUE
DESCRIPTION:A mansion. A storm. Six strangers with secrets. And one very long night....Clue started life as a board game\, invented in 1940s England by Anthony E. Pratt and released in 1949 as Cluedo. (Americans shortened it to Clue.) In 1985\, Hollywood turned it into a movie\, and the studio did something wild: it sent three different endings to different theaters\, so audiences never knew which version they'd get. The film became a cult classic\, quoted endlessly by fans ever since....In 2017\, playwright Sandy Rustin brought the story to the stage\, with additional material by Hunter Foster and Eric Price. It premiered right here in Pennsylvania at the Bucks County Playhouse and has since become one of the most popular plays in the country\, topping the list of most-produced high school plays year after year....Here's the setup. It's 1954. Six guests arrive at a remote New England mansion\, each lured by a mysterious invitation and each hiding something they'd rather keep buried. A suspiciously polished butler welcomes them in. Then the lights go out\, the bodies start piling up\, and everyone becomes a suspect. Expect slamming doors\, frantic chases from room to room\, and a whole lot of finger-pointing as the guests race to figure out whodunit before they're next....This fall\, we're bringing you two full casts\, Blue and Gold\, alternating performances throughout the run. Same mansion\, same mystery\, two distinct takes on the madness. Our students are bringing so much to these roles that one cast simply wasn't enough. Come see one\, or come back and see both....Grab your magnifying glass and get your guesses ready. Just don't trust anyone....This production includes simulated gunshots....Friday\, October 30\, 7:30 pm (Gold Cast)...Saturday\, October 31\, 7:30 pm (Blue Cast)...Sunday\, November 1\, 2:00 pm (Gold Cast)...Friday\, November 6\, 7:30 pm (Gold Cast)...Saturday\, November 7\, 2:00 pm (Blue Cast)...Saturday\, November 7\, 7:30 pm (Gold Cast)...Sunday\, November 8\, 2:00 pm (Blue Cast)
LOCATION:Hillman Center - HCPA Dressing Rooms\, HCPA Green Room\, HCPA Kountz Theater\, HCPA Lower Lobby\, HCPA Upper Lobby
PRIORITY:0
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:129925217@www.shadysideacademy.org
DTSTAMP:20261118T195632Z
DTSTART:20261031T110000
DTEND:20261031T133000
SUMMARY:Goldstein Test Prep - Practice Tests
DESCRIPTION:Shady Side students will have the opportunity to take a free SAT and/or ACT practice test through Goldstein Test Prep. Students are welcome to try an SAT and an ACT in consecutive weekends to determine which might be the better fit. Tests are free to attend\, but please reserve a spot by registering with Mike Goldstein at mike.goldstein@goldsteintestprep.com or calling 412-874-7645.
LOCATION:Upper School Campus - SS Rowe 201\, SS Rowe 202
PRIORITY:0
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:129925084@www.shadysideacademy.org
DTSTAMP:20261118T195632Z
DTSTART:20261031T193000
DTEND:20261031T213000
SUMMARY:Senior School Fall Play: CLUE
DESCRIPTION:A mansion. A storm. Six strangers with secrets. And one very long night....Clue started life as a board game\, invented in 1940s England by Anthony E. Pratt and released in 1949 as Cluedo. (Americans shortened it to Clue.) In 1985\, Hollywood turned it into a movie\, and the studio did something wild: it sent three different endings to different theaters\, so audiences never knew which version they'd get. The film became a cult classic\, quoted endlessly by fans ever since....In 2017\, playwright Sandy Rustin brought the story to the stage\, with additional material by Hunter Foster and Eric Price. It premiered right here in Pennsylvania at the Bucks County Playhouse and has since become one of the most popular plays in the country\, topping the list of most-produced high school plays year after year....Here's the setup. It's 1954. Six guests arrive at a remote New England mansion\, each lured by a mysterious invitation and each hiding something they'd rather keep buried. A suspiciously polished butler welcomes them in. Then the lights go out\, the bodies start piling up\, and everyone becomes a suspect. Expect slamming doors\, frantic chases from room to room\, and a whole lot of finger-pointing as the guests race to figure out whodunit before they're next....This fall\, we're bringing you two full casts\, Blue and Gold\, alternating performances throughout the run. Same mansion\, same mystery\, two distinct takes on the madness. Our students are bringing so much to these roles that one cast simply wasn't enough. Come see one\, or come back and see both....Grab your magnifying glass and get your guesses ready. Just don't trust anyone....This production includes simulated gunshots....Friday\, October 30\, 7:30 pm (Gold Cast)...Saturday\, October 31\, 7:30 pm (Blue Cast)...Sunday\, November 1\, 2:00 pm (Gold Cast)...Friday\, November 6\, 7:30 pm (Gold Cast)...Saturday\, November 7\, 2:00 pm (Blue Cast)...Saturday\, November 7\, 7:30 pm (Gold Cast)...Sunday\, November 8\, 2:00 pm (Blue Cast)
LOCATION:Hillman Center - HCPA Dressing Rooms\, HCPA Green Room\, HCPA Kountz Theater\, HCPA Lower Lobby\, HCPA Upper Lobby
PRIORITY:0
END:VEVENT
