UID:129925063@www.shadysideacademy.org
DTSTAMP:20261118T195632Z
DTSTART:20261105T080000
DTEND:20261105T120000
SUMMARY:The American Mathematics Competition
DESCRIPTION:The American Mathematics Competition (AMC) is the first step in a series of prestigious mathematics exams hosted by the Mathematical Association of America (MAA) to find talent for the International Mathematical Olympiad (IMO). Students who are in ninth or tenth grade have the option to take the AMC10\, while older students will take the AMC12. Both exams are 75 minutes in length and cover 25 multiple-choice questions that delve deeply into advanced algebra\, geometry\, trigonometry\, and some calculus. The questions require students to engage with critical thinking and rigorous "out of the box" problem-solving for the duration of the exam. Students who score high enough on the AMC10 or AMC12 will then be able to register for the secondary step\, the American Invitational Mathematics Exam (AIME) in February.
LOCATION:Upper School Campus - RMS Dining Hall
PRIORITY:0
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:129922464@www.shadysideacademy.org
DTSTAMP:20261118T195632Z
DTSTART:20261105T100000
DTEND:20261105T103000
SUMMARY:Personal Finance Class Session
DESCRIPTION:At Shady Side\, learning is meant to have real-world impact and value. This Personal Finance course is designed with that in mind. Students will engage with practical topics such as managing money\, understanding credit\, and making informed financial decisions. The goal is not only knowledge\, but confidence and judgment in real situations they will soon encounter.  All students will complete a Personal Finance course as part of graduation requirements during their tenth grade year. This aligns with new mandated requirements across Pennsylvania and reflects Shady Side's continued focus on preparing students for life beyond the classroom.
LOCATION:Hillman Center - HCPA Rauh Theater
PRIORITY:0
END:VEVENT
