DTSTAMP:20261118T195632Z
DTSTART:20261117T083000
DTEND:20261117T093000
SUMMARY:UPA Parent Book Club
DESCRIPTION:Middle School and Senior School Parents are invited to join the newly combined Upper School Parents Book Club. This book club provides a unique opportunity for parents to meet senior school faculty and staff who recommend a book for the group to read\, and then to attend one of the meetings to facilitate a discussion of their chosen book. The book club meetings are held in the Class of 1966 Memorial Hall Library in Rowe Hall. Senior School Band Instructor\, Ian Hughes\, will lead a discussion on the book Coyoteland: A Novel by Vanessa Hua - a witty\, yet empathetic\, story about suburban drama\, relationships\, and scandal. All parents are welcome\, whether you are new to the group or a returning participant and whether you have read the book or not. For more information\, please contact Kirsten Marcel (kmarcel99@sbcglobal.net) or Veronica Dristas (dristas@pitt.edu).
LOCATION:Upper School Campus - SS Memorial Library
PRIORITY:0
END:VEVENT
