BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:129925070@www.shadysideacademy.org
DTSTAMP:20261118T195632Z
DTSTART:20261203T190000
DTEND:20261203T203000
SUMMARY:Beyond the Game: Navigating NCAA Recruiting
DESCRIPTION:Is your child interested in playing sports at the collegiate level? Join us for an engaging panel discussion designed to help parents of student-athletes better understand the college athletics recruiting process. Hear directly from experienced professionals and members of the SSA community as they share insights into NCAA recruiting\, what college coaches look for\, when students should begin preparing\, and how families can support the journey. Whether your child is actively pursuing collegiate athletics or beginning to explore their possibilities\, you'll leave with a valuable perspective\, practical guidance\, and answers to your questions. Confirmed panelists: Josh Centor\, Carnegie Mellon University Director of Athletics\, Andrew McMillan\, Associate Director of Admission at Carnegie Mellon University\, Erika Cooper\, Shady Side Academy Coach/Parent of Recruited Student Athletes. Registration is requested: https://events.veracross.com/ssa/159-athletics-recruiting
LOCATION:Upper School Campus - SS Memorial Library
PRIORITY:0
END:VEVENT
